  "description": "Rowan Fitzgerald welcomes you to this exceptional two double bedroom home, extended to the rear to give fantastic living accommodation and ideally positioned with lovely river walks. Previously owner occupied and with no onward chain, No. 67 has been well cared for and is ideal for first time buyers, downsizers or investment purchasers. On entering the hall door there is a bright entrance hall with the living room on the immediate right. Beyond the hall is a large sitting room with feature fireplace creating the focal point, with double doors to the extended kitchen/dining room, which in turn leads to the garden. Upstairs there are two double bedrooms and a shower room. Outside there is a low maintenance garden to the rear with parking at the front.  \nThe location is second to none, within a short walk of Limerick City with its vibrant centre offering excellent bars, restaurants, cafes and shops. King Johns Castle and Clancy Strand are both just a short walk from the house, as is Thomond Park and the GAA Gaelic Grounds, as well as TUS/LIT campus. Shops and retail centres on the Ennis Road are also just a short distance away.  For more information or to arrange a viewing, please contact Rachael on 061-279423 or email reply to this advert.\nDisclaimer: These particulars and terms are provided by Rowan Fitzgerald Auctioneers with the understanding that all negotiations regarding the mentioned property must be conducted exclusively through them. While every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy of the information provided, Rowan Fitzgerald Auctioneers makes no warranties, express or implied, regarding the particulars or any representations made about the property. The details in this brochure do not form any part of a contract. Prospective purchasers or lessees are advised to independently verify all details to their satisfaction. Rowan Fitzgerald Auctioneers shall not be held responsible for any loss or expenses incurred in visiting the property, including but not limited to instances where the property is found to be unsuitable, already sold, let, or withdrawn from the market.",
